WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.486 --> 00:00:05.976
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:14.340
INES TORRES: Pyramids are one of the most

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:18.840
common of all human architectural forms, and one of the most stable.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.910
But the reason for building a pyramid is also

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.790
related to a set of religious and funerary beliefs

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.800
that the Egyptian espoused.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.900
Some of these beliefs are intimately connected

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.420
to the Egyptians' own landscape.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:33.360
Until very recently, the Nile waters would annually

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:37.860
flood and recede, leaving behind deposits of fertile silt,

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:41.910
creating a visual effect that associated floods and mounds of earth

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:44.670
to the regeneration and conception of life.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:47.610
The pyramidal form represents quite well the visual idea

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:51.810
of the primeval mound of creation emerging from the fertile floods.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:56.190
In fact, some early Egyptian temples kept a miniature primeval mound,

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:58.620
which could take the form of a pyramid carved

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.310
from a block of stone called Benben.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:04.530
This was a representation of the first mound

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:08.790
of land, which appeared after the waters of creation receded.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:12.090
From this primeval mound, and according to the Egyptian view,

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:15.120
the sun rose for the first time, giving life and warmth

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.950
to the newly created Earth.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.730
Representations of the Benben incorporated the very power of life

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:22.110
itself.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:25.410
As such, monuments had not only aesthetic value,

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:29.400
but were also imbued with powerful religious symbolism.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.860
The primeval mound, or Benben, was sometimes

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.340
included within the tomb's structure.

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:36.750
And in this context, they were believed to provide

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:41.220
the power necessary for the spiritual rebirth of the tomb owner.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:44.850
The rectangular mud brick structure, known as mastaba,

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:49.050
seems to have been connected to the representation of the primeval mound.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:52.680
Pyramids are, therefore, representations of the Benben mound,

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:54.990
but on a monumental scale.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.660
Benben was also the name given to the pyramidion,

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:00.770
or the tip of a pyramid or obelisk.

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:05.490
Both the Benben and the pyramids symbolized the rays of the sun.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:08.580
According to the Pyramid Texts, which were, nevertheless, found

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:12.020
engraved in later pyramids, the king would mount up to the sky

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:14.400
by using the sun rays as a ramp.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:19.140
Thus, the pyramid was also a place of physical and spiritual transformation,

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.570
which allowed the king to ascend to heaven

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:25.590
and join the solar god during his daily rebirth.

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:29.370
It is worth noting that the original appearance of the Pyramids of Giza

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:34.170
was very different from today, since at least the Pyramids of Khufu and Khafre

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:37.170
would have been encased in shining white limestone, which

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:42.330
would have reflected the sun's rays, and created a splendid visual effect.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:45.000
In addition, the pyramid complex also served

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.840
as a model of the hierarchical structure of the Egyptian culture,

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:52.330
with the king's pyramid towering over all other structures,

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:56.100
and surrounded most closely by his most important officials.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.890
This means that the significance of such cemeteries

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:01.980
is not only religious or funerary, but it also

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:05.510
reflects the practices of an entire society.

